# J9 — Jobs / steer queue
# Launch work, open jobs, queue a second tool while the first runs, then
# scoped-cancel. Known risk: steer-queue starvation (branch review).
# Keyless variant rides the offline demo; the queue window is short, so
# judge captures and re-run keyed for a wider window.
name: Jobs and steer queue
cwd: @TMP_TARGET
env-unset: ANTHROPIC_API_KEY OPENAI_API_KEY
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1
launch:
wait-for: 25 CHOOSE A TARGET
submit: demo
wait-for: 10 RUN FOCUS
# Queue a tool while the demo run is live — should land in the steer queue.
type: queue run secret-scan:scan {}
keys: Enter
wait: 0.1
snap: steer-queued-mid-run
expect: queued: 1 pending
ask: Queueing while busy — did the shell say the tool was QUEUED (pending), not silently dropped and not falsely running?
submit: jobs
wait: 2
snap: jobs-live-and-queued
ask: Jobs view — one live run max; queued steer items render as pending; live vs. stale-disk rows labeled truthfully?
wait: 3
snap: jobs-after-drain
ask: Steer drain — after the live run finished, did the queued tool actually dispatch (chain → plan → steer order), or did it starve?
submit: queue
wait: 2
snap: queue-view
expect-not: unknown command
ask: `queue` — does the steer queue surface show honest pending/dispatched state, and does `jobs -k <id>` (scoped cancel) look reachable from here?
